# Section copy vs lib data

Structured, repeatable records belong in `lib/`. Section-level prose belongs in the matching section component as HTML — not as a string array next to those records.

`lib/about.ts` exports `aboutInterests` (and href/id helpers) only. The About biography is a `<p>` in `components/about.tsx`. The Home intro is already a `<p>` in `components/home.tsx`. Do not add `aboutBio`-style copy arrays to content modules.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — section copy in the data file
export const aboutBio: string[] = [
  "This half of the page is less about what I ship...",
]

{aboutBio.map((paragraph) => (
  <p key={paragraph}>{paragraph}</p>
))}

// ✅ GOOD — nested records stay in lib
export const aboutInterests: AboutInterest[] = [
  { id: "hockey", title: "Montreal Canadiens", caption: "..." },
]

// ✅ GOOD — biography is HTML in the section component
<p className="mt-8 max-w-md text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground sm:text-base">
  This half of the page is less about what I ship and more about how I
  spend time when I’m not in an editor.
</p>
```

Still keep experiences, projects, skills, education, and interest prints as typed arrays in `lib/`. Do not inline those records in components.
